<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    `previewLayout` for the month calendar. See widget_preview_log_period for why the colours are
    literal and the content is sample data.

    The grid is March 2026 because it starts on a Sunday and runs 31 days, so a Sunday-first layout
    fills exactly five rows — a real month rather than a month shaped to fit. Marks are the widget's
    own: recorded period 1-5, fertile window 12-17, estimated ovulation on the 16th, today the 8th.
    Today is bold here but not underlined; a static layout has no equivalent of the live widget's
    TextDecoration.Underline without spans.

    NestedWeights and SmallSp are suppressed for the grid rather than designed around. The launcher
    inflates this file once, at a fixed size, to draw a thumbnail — the extra measure pass a 7x5 grid
    of weights costs is not a frame budget anyone is watching. The 10sp weekday initials match what
    the live widget draws at this size; growing them only in the preview would misrepresent it.
-->
